('key', [
    "Communication = a **two-way** process; it is complete only with **feedback**. *Communicare* = 'to share'.",
    "Elements: **Sender \u2192 encoding \u2192 message \u2192 channel \u2192 receiver \u2192 decoding \u2192 feedback**, with **noise** and **context** acting throughout.",
    "Types: verbal (oral, written), non-verbal, visual; formal/informal; downward/upward/horizontal/diagonal; intrapersonal/interpersonal/group/mass; therapeutic.",
    "**Non-verbal communication often outweighs words** \u2014 face, eyes, posture, gesture, touch, space, tone, silence, appearance.",
    "**SOLER** = the attentive listening posture; **active/empathic listening** is the professional standard.",
    "**Empathy \u2260 sympathy.** Empathy understands and retains objectivity; sympathy pities and risks exhaustion.",
    "Barriers = **physical, physiological, psychological, semantic, cultural, organisational, personal, perceptual.**",
    "Effective communication = the **7 C's**: Clear, Concise, Concrete, Correct, Coherent, Complete, Courteous.",
    "**SBAR** (Situation, Background, Assessment, Recommendation) is the structured tool for talking to clinicians; always finish with a **read-back** and **documentation**.",
    "The **assertive** style is the professional ideal \u2014 not passive, not aggressive.",
    "Legal maxim: **'Not documented, not done.'**"
]),

